Appendix A. Provenance verification kernel (H4)

A.1 Representation and well-formedness

The kernel represents the registry as a finite set of items with unique identifiers, a dependency relation restricted to edges whose target is present, and a propagation operator defined as a total function on the item set. Both soundness and completeness are proved. No sorry occurs; the only classical assumption is propositional extensionality through Classical.propDecidable, which is recorded in the trusted base (Appendix J).

```lean
import Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic
import Mathlib.Data.Finset.Image
import Mathlib.Data.Set.Basic

namespace Protocol.Provenance

open Classical

inductive KnowledgeStatus : Type where
  | Valid | Reexamine | Invalidated
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr

structure ClaimId where
  id : Nat
  deriving DecidableEq, Hashable, Repr

structure KnowledgeItem where
  id : ClaimId
  status : KnowledgeStatus
  dependencies : Finset ClaimId
  deriving DecidableEq

structure ProvenanceGraph where
  claims : Finset KnowledgeItem
  closed : ∀ k ∈ claims, ∀ d ∈ k.dependencies, ∃ k' ∈ claims, k'.id = d
  idInj  : ∀ k ∈ claims, ∀ k' ∈ claims, k.id = k'.id → k = k'

variable (g : ProvenanceGraph)

/-- Transitive dependency closure (non-reflexive). -/
inductive DependsOn : ClaimId → ClaimId → Prop where
  | direct {p c : ClaimId} (k : KnowledgeItem) (hk : k ∈ g.claims)
      (hid : k.id = c) (hp : p ∈ k.dependencies) : DependsOn p c
  | tail {p m c : ClaimId} (h₁ : DependsOn p m) (h₂ : DependsOn m c) :
      DependsOn p c

/-- An item is affected by an invalidation set if some root reaches it. -/
def affected (roots : Finset ClaimId) (c : ClaimId) : Prop :=
  ∃ r ∈ roots, DependsOn g r c
```

A.2 Propagation operator

```lean
noncomputable def newStatus (roots : Finset ClaimId) (k : KnowledgeItem) :
    KnowledgeStatus :=
  if k.id ∈ roots then KnowledgeStatus.Invalidated
  else if affected g roots k.id then KnowledgeStatus.Reexamine
  else k.status

noncomputable def propagate (roots : Finset ClaimId) : ProvenanceGraph where
  claims := g.claims.image (fun k => { k with status := newStatus g roots k })
  closed := by
    intro k hk d hd
    rw [Finset.mem_image] at hk
    obtain ⟨k₀, hk₀, rfl⟩ := hk
    simp only at hd
    obtain ⟨k₁, hk₁, hid⟩ := g.closed k₀ hk₀ d hd
    exact ⟨{ k₁ with status := newStatus g roots k₁ }, Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ hk₁, hid⟩
  idInj := by
    intro k hk k' hk' hid
    rw [Finset.mem_image] at hk hk'
    obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := hk
    obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := hk'
    simp only at hid
    have hab : a.id = b.id := hid
    rw [g.idInj a ha b hb hab]
```

A.3 Soundness

```lean
lemma newStatus_ne_valid (roots : Finset ClaimId) (k : KnowledgeItem)
    (h : affected g roots k.id) :
    newStatus g roots k ≠ KnowledgeStatus.Valid := by
  unfold newStatus
  by_cases hroot : k.id ∈ roots
  · rw [if_pos hroot]; exact KnowledgeStatus.noConfusion
  · rw [if_neg hroot, if_pos h]; exact KnowledgeStatus.noConfusion

theorem h4_soundness (roots : Finset ClaimId) (item : KnowledgeItem)
    (hitem : item ∈ (propagate g roots).claims)
    (root : ClaimId) (hroot : root ∈ roots) (hdep : DependsOn g root item.id) :
    item.status ≠ KnowledgeStatus.Valid := by
  rw [propagate, Finset.mem_image] at hitem
  obtain ⟨k, _, rfl⟩ := hitem
  exact newStatus_ne_valid g roots k ⟨root, hroot, hdep⟩
```

The theorem states: any item reachable from an invalidated root by a chain of active dependencies carries status Invalidated or Reexamine, never Valid. Because the proof has no sorry, the obligation is discharged by kernel type-checking alone, subject to the trusted base of Appendix J.

A.4 Completeness (Correction C2)

The completeness invariant stated in §4.3 must be restricted: a root is invalidated even though it is not transitively dependent on itself, since DependsOn is non-reflexive. The corrected invariant is therefore stated for non-root, non-affected items, and is the one verified below.

```lean
lemma newStatus_eq_of_unaffected (roots : Finset ClaimId) (k : KnowledgeItem)
    (hroot : k.id ∉ roots) (hunaff : ¬ affected g roots k.id) :
    newStatus g roots k = k.status := by
  unfold newStatus
  rw [if_neg hroot, if_neg hunaff]

theorem h4_completeness (roots : Finset ClaimId) (k : KnowledgeItem)
    (hk : k ∈ g.claims) (hvalid : k.status = KnowledgeStatus.Valid)
    (hroot : k.id ∉ roots) (hunaff : ¬ affected g roots k.id) :
    ({ k with status := newStatus g roots k } : KnowledgeItem).status
      = KnowledgeStatus.Valid := by
  show newStatus g roots k = KnowledgeStatus.Valid
  rw [newStatus_eq_of_unaffected g roots k hroot hunaff, hvalid]
```

Completeness eliminates the degenerate implementation that invalidates every item: such an operator satisfies soundness vacuously but violates completeness on any item outside the affected set. Together, the two theorems certify that propagate is the intended transformation and not merely a safe one.

A.5 Cost and complexity note

affected is decided by classical propositional decidability over a finite closure; in the extracted implementation it is computed by breadth-first search over Finset ClaimId, with cost \mathcal{O}(|V_K| + |E_K|) per root set. The kernel does not certify asymptotic cost; performance is reported empirically under the latency budget of Experiment 2.

