J.1.2 Audit procedure

For each theorem T, the artifact runs #print axioms T and records the transitive closure. Certification requires the closure to be a subset of the trusted base. The artifact also runs set_option autoImplicit false, set_option pp.universes true, and a scan for sorry, admit, native_decide, and @[implemented_by] in the audited files. The CI log is published with the paper artifact, and the audit table is reproduced for every theorem named in the main text: h4_soundness, h4_completeness, forward_invariance, shield_safe, shield_forward_invariance.

J.1.3 What the audit does and does not establish

The audit establishes that the theorems follow from the trusted base. It does not establish that the Lean statements faithfully formalize the intended notions of invalidation or safety, nor that any implementation instantiates them (Appendix I). Fidelity of formalization is a review obligation; conformance is an empirical obligation. Neither is discharged by the audit.

